WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.348
Every danger here is a way a well-meant
change goes wrong in production,

2
00:00:04.348 --> 00:00:06.200
and each has a guard in the code.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.286
The worst is order: remove
standing Owner before the eligible

4
00:00:10.286 --> 00:00:14.212
role exists and someone loses
access in the middle of a task.

5
00:00:14.212 --> 00:00:19.375
Close behind is the automation removing
its own access halfway through a run.

6
00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:23.950
Others are quieter: a resource group
nobody listed keeps its defaults, an

7
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.686
authentication context points
at a policy that isn't there,

8
00:00:27.686 --> 00:00:29.363
or a typo lands unreviewed.

9
00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:31.806
The pattern is the same as before:

10
00:00:31.806 --> 00:00:35.500
a dry run by default, and
rules that run every time.
